<rml>
<head>
	<title>Friends</title>
	<link type="text/template" href="../shell.rml"/>
	<style>
		.friends-columns { display: flex; flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 40dp; margin-top: 40dp; }
		.friends-column { flex: 1 1 360dp; max-width: 560dp; }
		.friends-item { padding: 14dp 0dp; border-bottom: 1dp var(--line); }
		.friends-item-title { font-size: 15dp; font-weight: 600; line-height: 20dp; }
		.friends-item-text { margin-top: 4dp; font-size: 13dp; line-height: 19dp; color: var(--text2); }
	</style>
</head>
<!-- Friends (docs/DESIGN.md 7.3): arrives with Xerces accounts in M5. Until
     then this page says what is off in this build (D14) and what will come,
     and nothing on it talks to a network. -->
<body template="shell">
<div class="page">
	<div class="page-title">Friends</div>
	<div class="page-sub">Friends, presence and invites arrive with Xerces accounts. Until then Xerces sends nothing about you anywhere, and joining a friend works through Servers with their address.</div>

	<div class="friends-columns">
		<div class="friends-column">
			<div class="label section-label">Off in this build</div>
			<div class="friends-item">
				<div class="friends-item-title">Friend presence and invites</div>
				<div class="friends-item-text">BOIII sent your friend code to its masters every few seconds. Xerces builds leave that out.</div>
			</div>
			<div class="friends-item">
				<div class="friends-item-title">Connecting through BOIII's servers</div>
				<div class="friends-item-text">The rendezvous that helped two players behind routers find each other is off too. Direct connect and LAN still work.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="friends-column">
			<div class="label section-label">Coming with accounts</div>
			<div class="friends-item">
				<div class="friends-item-title">Friend requests, presence and parties</div>
				<div class="friends-item-text">Optional, with privacy settings and block and report.</div>
			</div>
			<div class="friends-item">
				<div class="friends-item-title">Invites that bring the right mods</div>
				<div class="friends-item-text">An invite carries the pack, so Xerces can tell you which Workshop items to get in Steam first.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="section toolbar">
		<button id="friends-servers" class="outline default-focus"><span>Open Servers</span></button>
		<button id="friends-home" class="link"><span>Back to Home</span></button>
	</div>
</div>
</body>
</rml>
